From fae8503b2abfbc0f802c00e1c50bde5d470bbbe7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:36:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 361/365] DOS-PORT: patch 0361 -- script VM slice 3: six
 superinstructions and two divisions off the hot path

MMD's hottest instruction sequences, each fused into one handler that lives in the opcode slot of
its first instruction (entering the group anywhere else runs the single handlers, so jumps into a
group stay exact): farcall (farpush; setfuncargs; movl ax,IMPORT; farcall; farsubsp), localload and
localstore (mov sp,mar; subi mar,K; memread4/memwrite4), pushmovlpop, popbinmov (pop bx; sub|add|
cmpeq|gte; mov bx,ax) and cmpmovjz. DOSAGS_VM_FUSE=<mask> selects them (default all six, 0x3F;
fastnofuse/fastgeneric use none). Two divisions by sizeof(...) go: SystemImports::GetByIndexFast()
compares byte offsets instead, and the far-call stack pop count is computed without a division.

Lab-only (-DDOSAGS_VMTRACE): DOSAGS_VM_SHADOW=1 replays every superinstruction through the stepper
on a snapshot and compares; the line/call-point digest (vmsync, folded at sourceline, farcall, call
and ret) is the comparison for fused arms, whose per-instruction trace differs by construction.

Lab (docs/lab/VM-SLICE3.md): shadow 0 mismatches over ~4.66M superinstruction executions; digests
EQUAL on the four fixtures; aq-journeys 10/10; MMD CS 9.256 -> 4.308 ms/tick at fixed 40k (2.15x).
486: round E 91.52 / 91.56% displayed (slice 2 86.94%); round C4 falsified the 8 KB cache suspect
(masks 0x3F/0x03/0x00: 90.16 / 88.72 / 87.52%), so all six stay.

